# All user state lives under memory/, which is a git
# repository of its own once bin/hostwarden-init has run: the
# workspace of an operations install. It is never part of
# this repository, in solo use or in a team; a team shares it
# through a remote of its own. The templates it starts from
# live in templates/memory/.
memory/

# Project history (auto-maintained by Claude Code).
HISTORY.md

# macOS noise.
.DS_Store

# hostwarden-doctor's symlink probe, should it ever be interrupted.
.link-probe.*

# Claude Code: everything under .claude/ is ignored except the shared
# configuration named below. Claude Code keeps adding personal files
# there — settings.local.json, worktrees, locks, scheduled tasks, a
# subagent's local memory — and a new one must not reach this public
# repo before anyone notices. The reverse mistake, a new shared file
# ignored, is loud: `git add` refuses it, and instructions-test.sh
# fails when a tracked file matches these rules.
#
# settings.local.json above all: Claude Code appends an allow rule
# to it every time you approve a command, so it fills up with the
# literal commands you ran, hostnames and all. settings.json is the
# shared, hostname-free half. `skills` has no trailing slash: it is
# a symlink, which git stores as a file.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills
!.claude/agent-memory/
!.claude/workflows/

# Personal Claude Code instructions; CLAUDE.md is the shared half.
CLAUDE.local.md
